  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indonesia Investment and Trade Reforms DPL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the Investment and Trade Reforms Development Policy Financing in Indonesia is to reform Indonesia&apos;s investment and trade policies to support economic recovery and transformation. The operation is structured around the following pillars: Pillar A: attracting private investment, particularly foreign direct investment (FDI) by: (i) opening more sectors to private investment, particularly FDI; (ii) facilitating a more adequate supply of high-skilled professionals for the labor market needs; and (iii) stimulating private investment in solar energy. Pillar B: reforming trade policy to support competitiveness and the economic recovery by: (i) increasing accessibility and affordability of 18 widely consumed food commodities and raw materials; and (ii) facilitating access to manufacturing inputs.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the reform of Indonesia&apos;s investment and trade policies in support of economic recovery and transformation.</narrative>
  </description>
